# Commit messages

When creating git commits, always use this pattern:

```text
type(scope): short summary

- Point of change
- Point of change
```

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`
- Include a scope (e.g. `layout`, `api`, `overview`)
- Summary: imperative, concise
- Body: bullet points with `-` listing the concrete changes
